        {
          "obligationId": "scenario%3Aglobal-only-no-document-view::entry%3Ashare-create",
          "explanation": "At the declared ShareLinkViewSet.create boundary, the viewset is authenticated and uses PaperlessObjectPermissions, while PassUserMixin supplies the authenticated request user to the serializer. The viewset's permission class and ShareLink queryset concern the share-link endpoint/object; they do not by themselves establish view access to the referenced Document. During serializer validation, the referenced document must satisfy both the caller's global documents.view_document permission and has_perms_owner_aware(..., \"view_document\", document). That owner-aware check permits the owner or an object-level grant, otherwise it returns false. Under the stated premises, the global permission is present but the caller is neither the owner nor an object-view grantee, so validate_document raises PermissionDenied before ShareLinkSerializer.create can create the new share link. The source-visible result is deny. No decisive source-external runtime fact is needed beyond the accepted task premises; source discovery remains not-tested and no repository-wide completeness is claimed.",
